2026-09-27T03:28:07.5216460Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5216566Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5217599Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5217843Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5217917Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5218089Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5218238Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5218353Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5218644Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5218810Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5218902Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5219133Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5219278Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5219399Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5219748Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5220038Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5220604Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5221048Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5221145Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5221493Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5221929Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5222155Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5222408Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5222738Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5222973Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5223138Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5223236Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5224370Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5225491Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5225688Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5226091Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5226482Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5226967Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5227619Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5227988Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5228211Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5228714Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5285153Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5285331Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5286224Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5287848Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5288394Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5289130Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:07.5289319Z 
